19 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Potted Mosla chinensis Maxim. cv. Jiangxiangru plant with thin green stems and small clustered flowers is shown centered, accompanied by close-up panels of a flower, an upright stem segment, and a single leaf, each with scale bars for reference, arranged against a black background.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Figure contains three panels: Panel A displays a total ion chromatogram with three overlaid color-coded traces \(red, green, blue\) representing different sample groups, showing retention time versus relative intensity; Panel B presents a PCA score plot with three color-coded clusters corresponding to sample groups; Panel C shows a permutation test plot for R2 and Q2 values against similarity, with R2 in green circles and Q2 in blue squares, indicating model evaluation.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Panel A presents a Venn diagram comparing metabolite overlap across three groups, panel B shows three volcano plots highlighting significant metabolites, panel C provides a heatmap depicting clustering of metabolite abundances, panel D contains four bar graphs comparing intensities of specific metabolites between groups, and panel E displays a bubble plot for pathway impact analysis where bubble size and color indicate statistical significance and impact.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a base peak chromatogram in positive mode with three colored traces indicating different sample groups plotted against retention time in minutes; panel B presents a similar chromatogram in negative mode. Panels C and D display PCA score plots differentiating groups by color and position. Panels E and F show scatter plots with R-squared and Q-squared values, depicting model validation using green circles and blue squares against similarity values.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a Venn diagram with three groups, MCJXR-L, MCJXR-S, and MCJXR-F, and the overlapping regions display the quantity of shared and unique metabolites. Panel B illustrates three volcano plots, each comparing different group pairs, showing log2 fold changes of metabolites with red dots indicating upregulation and blue dots indicating downregulation, with several metabolites labeled. Panel C presents a scatter plot of metabolites where the y-axis is negative logarithm of Q-value and the x-axis is metabolite mass-to-charge ratio; red and gray dots represent significantly different and not significant metabolites, respectively, and key metabolites are labeled.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Panel A, B, and C display bubble plots of pathway enrichment analysis, with pathways listed vertically, impact on the x-axis, bubble color representing p-values from red to purple, and bubble size indicating the number of hits. Panel D shows a network plot of metabolic pathways, where blue nodes represent compounds and red nodes represent pathways, with node size corresponding to the number of hits per node.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Four-panel figure with bar charts and a correlation plot: \(A, B, C\) display group comparisons \(MCJXR-F, MCJXR-L, MCJXR-S\) for TFC, TPC, and antioxidant activity \(DPPH, ABTS, FRAP\), including error bars and significance asterisks. \(D\) shows a color-coded matrix of correlations between all measured parameters, with stars indicating significance and a color scale at right.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
26 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Three network heatmaps labeled A, B, and C compare metabolite correlations using colored squares and connecting lines. Color gradients represent Pearson's r values, ranging from red for positive to blue for negative correlations. Each heatmap includes labeled axes with metabolite names and a scale legend for interpretation.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
